      "utf8": "completely? Well, unfortunately not. But it is in \nan infamously turbulent corner of the tech space.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The network effect of social media has worked in \ntheir favor for a long time, but it can also work  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against them. People go where their friends go. \nAnd I mean, how many of you actually have friends  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that still seriously use Facebook? It's also worth \nnoting the important little commercial detail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that people just [ __ ] hate Facebook. Polling \nfrom Pew last year found that around twothirds  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Americans view Zuckerberg unfavorably \nwith majorities of both parties agreeing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on it. So despite its rebrand, it has somehow \nmanaged to piss off both sides of politics,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which might be the closest thing to bipartisan \nconsensus this country has produced in a decade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leniency for the sake of maintaining a brand isn't \nas likely as it might be for companies that still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have some supporters. There is also really nothing \nstopping Facebook or Instagram or WhatsApp being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sold off to someone else or spun out into their \nown companies to cover these financial shortfalls.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a 2018 email that surfaced during the \nantitrust trial, he wrote that there was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a non-trivial chance the company would be forced \nto spin out Instagram within a decade anyway. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I guess the point is Meta can probably pay its way \nout of most of these problems individually. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134240,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real question is whether it can afford all of them \nfrom everywhere all at once. Now, I don't want to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get too caught up in wishful thinking, but go and \nwatch this video next to try and figure out how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this possibly ends well. And don't forget to like \nand subscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
